# Cursor AI Workspace Rules & Context Directives

# ======================================================================
# 1. MASTER CONTEXT POINTERS
# ======================================================================
# Direct Cursor AI to primary architectural documentation:
# Primary Blueprint:   @ARCHITECTURE.md
# Project Directives:  @project-preferences.md
# Discovery Findings:  @DISCOVERY_REPORT.md
# Agent Operational Rules: @.agents/rules/persona-and-principles.md

# ======================================================================
# 2. IGNORED DIRECTORIES & PATH EXCLUSIONS
# ======================================================================
# Exclude build outputs, dependencies, and generated caches from indexing context:
ignore_directories:
  - .nuxt/
  - .output/
  - node_modules/
  - dist/
  - .idea/
  - .git/

# ======================================================================
# 3. STRICT ARCHITECTURAL GUARDRAILS
# ======================================================================
# Rule 1: Use <script setup lang="ts"> exclusively in all Vue SFCs.
# Rule 2: Zero `any` types permitted. Strict type safety across function parameters, props, and API contracts.
# Rule 3: No direct DOM manipulation (document.getElementById, querySelector, innerHTML). Use ref / reactive.
# Rule 4: Component state isolation — Props Down (read-only), Emits Up (defineEmits).

# ======================================================================
# 4. NUXT 3 & SUPABASE CONVENTIONS
# ======================================================================
# Nuxt Directory Layout:
# - pages/       -> Route views
# - layouts/     -> App layout shells
# - components/  -> Auto-imported Vue components
# - composables/ -> Reusable reactive state hooks (useMovieCatalog.ts, useAuth.ts)
# - server/api/  -> Express / Node server endpoint handlers
#
# Supabase Integration:
# - Access client via useSupabaseClient()
# - Guard authenticated routes using useSupabaseUser() in Nuxt middleware
# - Type all database entity responses using TypeScript interfaces

# ======================================================================
# 5. CONTEXT SYNCHRONIZATION & SKILL ACCESS
# ======================================================================
# To access newly generated skills (.agents/skills/), project preferences, or cross-tool changes:
# Always check `git diff` and `git status` when auditing modified workspace state.
